Your Structure (Entities, DTOs, Annotations) is Perfect (10/10).
But your Logic (The Calculation) has a Critical Math Error that will cause the code to crash or give the wrong answer.
You are calculating the percentage BEFORE you count the marks. It's like trying to calculate your exam score before you even write the exam!
❌ The Critical Logic Errors
1. The "Premature Calculation" Error 🧮
Look at this code block:
double totalMarks = 0;
int totalSubject = 0;

// 🚨 ERROR: You are dividing 0 by 0 here!
// At this line, totalMarks is 0. totalSubject is 0.
// Result = NaN (Not a Number) or Crash.
double percentage = (totalMarks / (totalSubject * 100.0)) * 100; 

for(SubjectMark item : studentRequest.getSubjects()) { ... }

The Fix: You must calculate the percentage AFTER the loop finishes, not before.
2. The "Confused Status" Error 😵‍💫
Inside your loop, you are trying to check for "DISTINCTION".
 * You cannot know if it is a Distinction until you have added up ALL the subjects.
 * Inside the Loop: Only check for failure (marks < 35).
 * Outside the Loop: Check for Distinction/First Class (using the final percentage).
✅ The 100% Correct Logic (The "Timeline")
Here is the correct flow. Read the comments to see WHEN things happen.
@Service
public class StudentService {

    @Autowired
    private StudentRepo studentRepo;

    public StudentResponce createStudent(StudentRequest studentRequest) {

        StudentResult studentResult = new StudentResult();
        studentResult.setStudentName(studentRequest.getStudentName());
        studentResult.setRollNumber(studentRequest.getRollNumber());
        studentResult.setSubjects(studentRequest.getSubjects());

        // --- STEP 1: PREPARE VARIABLES ---
        double totalMarks = 0;
        boolean hasFailed = false; // Flag to track if ANY subject failed
        int totalSubjects = studentRequest.getSubjects().size(); // Get count directly

        // --- STEP 2: THE LOOP (Calculate Total & Check Failures) ---
        for (SubjectMark item : studentRequest.getSubjects()) {
            
            // 1. Add to total
            totalMarks += item.getMarks();

            // 2. Check for "Deal Breaker" (Fail condition)
            if (item.getMarks() < 35) {
                hasFailed = true; 
            }
        }

        // --- STEP 3: CALCULATE PERCENTAGE (AFTER THE LOOP) ---
        // Now we have the real total!
        double percentage = (totalMarks / (totalSubjects * 100.0)) * 100;

        // --- STEP 4: DECIDE FINAL STATUS ---
        String finalStatus = "";

        if (hasFailed) {
            finalStatus = "FAIL"; // Failed one subject = FAIL
        } else if (percentage >= 75) {
            finalStatus = "DISTINCTION";
        } else if (percentage >= 60) {
            finalStatus = "FIRST CLASS";
        } else {
            finalStatus = "PASS";
        }

        // --- STEP 5: SAVE TO DB ---
        studentResult.setTotalMarks(totalMarks);
        studentResult.setPercentage(percentage);
        studentResult.setFinalResult(finalStatus); // Save the status!

        StudentResult savedData = studentRepo.save(studentResult);

        // --- STEP 6: RESPONSE ---
        StudentResponce response = new StudentResponce();
        response.setStudentId(savedData.getId());
        response.setStudentName(savedData.getStudentName());
        response.setTotalMarks(savedData.getTotalMarks());
        response.setPercentage(savedData.getPercentage());
        response.setFinalResult(savedData.getFinalResult());

        return response;
    }
}

🧠 The Lesson
Order of Operations matters.
 * Loop first: Collect all the data (Sum the marks).
 * Calculate second: Do the math (Percentage).
 * Judge third: Decide the result (Pass/Fail/Distinction).
You cannot Judge before you Loop!
Do you see how moving the percentage line to the bottom fixes the math problem?
